Splits the remainder of the spike in two so a truncated run loses at most
half: this brief takes the migration to a green workspace and nothing else,
and brief-501 will swap the representation and measure it.

The stop-loss is re-keyed from reason to progress, which is the correction
brief-499 earned: a non-Copy migration emits only ownership errors, so "the
same reason twice" fires on a repair that is converging. It now stops only
when a pass fails to reduce the distinct count, or when an error appears that
is not an ownership error — which would mean semantics had started to move.

Two things the last run discovered are written in rather than left to be
rediscovered: rum-core and rum-syntax declare rum-runtime as a dev-dependency,
so the dependency order inverts for test targets and their fallout is
invisible until rum-runtime compiles; and the set of types forced to drop
derive(Copy) is the transitive closure Symbol's Copy-ness was holding up, so
it is now a deliverable rather than a side effect.

