Subject: [PATCH 04/10] docs: brief-501, swap the representation and measure
 the three arms
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The measurement the spike exists for. It keeps the interner process-global
and leaking on purpose: A1's cost is the representation and A1's benefit is
the ownership, so if the representation alone is too expensive A1 falls here
and the ownership plumbing never has to be built.

Three arms rather than two. base to stage1 isolates what the ownership
migration alone costs, which theory says is zero because a Symbol clone is a
memcpy on the old layout; stage1 to candidate isolates the representation;
base to candidate is the total, and the total is what decides A1 because the
migration is not separable from it. A non-zero base-to-stage1 would mean the
migration moved something and every other number needs re-reading.

Ord is named as the brief's correctness trap: the id-equality fast path
cannot become a fingerprint-equality fast path, because a collision would
order two different symbols as Equal and corrupt every sorted structure.

The gate carries the exact expected failure set — 2473 passed, 1 failed, 57
ignored, the ownership-graph inventory row — and requires --no-fail-fast,
because brief-500's plain cargo test stopped at that failure and silently
left 208 tests unrun.

