 the ceiling trap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The first probe measured process startup: a Do over 200 000 iterations hits
the 100 000 iteration work limit, exits 1, and both arms read ~3.4M
instructions. That is the instrument this project's records have already
caught lying three times, so the brief now demands a scaling check — the
supplied workloads read 689 784 941 at N=25 000 and 1 376 080 468 at N=50 000,
a ratio of 1.995, which is what proves the loop ran at all.

With a workload that actually runs, the recipe repeats to 0.00005% within an
arm, and base to stage1 is +0.056%: the prediction that the ownership
migration alone costs about nothing holds, and it is not exactly zero. That
number is now the calibration point a candidate delta gets read against.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
