so the ownership migration is nearly free exactly as calibrated. stage1 to
candidate is +10.43% to +18.85% on every workload measured, and base to
candidate on ordinary evaluation is +14.33%. Allocations are fine: cold
intern adds 64000 for 16000 names, Module adds two per iteration, and warm
lookup and ordinary evaluation add none.

This project has rejected representation changes at 2-7%, 5-14% and 30%, and
accepted +0.714% and +0.606% only to remove a process kill. +14.33% on
ordinary evaluation is not close.

The worker states plainly what it did not isolate: the split among drop
state, hashing and equality, and other codegen effects. That split is the
next brief, because atomics and an equality demotion have entirely different
remedies and the number should not be ruled on until they are separated.

