brief-502 established the cost and said plainly it had not isolated the
cause. The two candidates have entirely different remedies — Arc refcount
traffic is intrinsic to any owning representation, while the equality
demotion from a dense-id fast accept to a pointer-then-fingerprint-then-text
compare might be repairable — so the number should not be ruled on until
they are separated.

Two variants, both correct programs rather than measurement hacks: V-arc
keeps the Arc and restores stage1's dense-id equality, which stays valid
because the interner is still global and still assigns one id per text; V-eq
keeps the fingerprint equality and puts the text back behind a leaked
&'static. Each must stay 24 bytes or it has introduced a confounder.

The sum check is part of the deliverable: a large residual would mean the two
changes interact in codegen, which is a third conclusion and not either
mechanism dominating.

It reuses brief-502's workload files, setup-subtraction triples and scripts
rather than rebuilding them, so every row lands beside the row it already
produced.

